{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:75427eb99000c117","name":"Skig Banos","source":{"id":"source:reference-75427eb99000c117","title":"Skig Banos","revision":23199,"timestamp":"2024-09-17T18:10:08Z","sha256":"e2616ec509af9e351d49ec005f6f589d2ff0f2b1e3a148a2ac4667d84440b517","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=23199","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Skig%20Banos&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-75427eb99000c117","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dawn of Defiance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dawn_of_Defiance"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["The Traitor's Gambit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Traitor%27s_Gambit","referenceId":"reference:b765bce19fabefc4"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As the heroes make their way across Blue Deck, they see a face that might be familiar. Any heroes who managed to notice the two ",{"tag":"a","children":["Imperial Informants"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Imperial_Informants"}," on the Promenade before ",{"tag":"a","children":["Maya"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Maya","referenceId":"reference:031e45c699d1aace"}," approached them now also notice a similarly dressed man on Blue Deck. In fact, any hero who succeeds on a DC 15 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," check realizes that this man was on the Promenade earlier but fled at the first sign of blaster fire. The man is Skig Banos, an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Imperial Informant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Imperial_Informant","referenceId":"reference:189d519975917abf"}," and world-class coward. With a mop of greasy black hair and a physique that is little more than skin hanging off bones, Skig looks a bit on the pathetic side. His beady eyes and oversized nose give him a more sinister edge, causing him to resemble a wild ",{"tag":"a","children":["Womp Rat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Womp_Rat","referenceId":"reference:132aef06340b6938"}," eager to escape captivity.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["If the heroes confront Skig, he immediately tries to escape. If the heroes manage to stop him without making too much of a ruckus, they should be able to interrogate him and get a bit more information about what is going on. Skig is too afraid of being harmed by the heroes to raise an alarm, and though his ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attitude"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attitude"}," begins as Unfriendly, a successful ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persuasion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persuasion","referenceId":"reference:196fbdc5f1823320"}," check can move him to Indifferent. Similarly, a successful ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persuasion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persuasion","referenceId":"reference:196fbdc5f1823320"}," check to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intimidate"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intimidate"}," Skig automatically moves his ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attitude"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attitude"}," 1 step farther toward Helpful, regardless of his ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attitude"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attitude"}," when the check is made.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["If Skig can be made Indifferent, he is willing to tell the heroes almost anything so that they will let him go. This includes lying to them- he makes ",{"tag":"a","children":["Deception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Deception","referenceId":"reference:17455029fb9994a3"}," checks every round until caught in a lie- and Skig's lies include that the Empire has discovered them, that the Empire has killed ",{"tag":"a","children":["Maya"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Maya","referenceId":"reference:031e45c699d1aace"},", and that he's just a merchant out for a walk on Blue Deck. An Indifferent Skig simply wants to get away, and he does everything he can to escape without getting killed or raising an alarm. Truthfully, Skig is equally scared of the Empire and fears that they will betray him at any time.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["If Skig can be made Friendly, he actually volunteers useful information. He knows that the Imperials were recently tipped off about contraband in the main docking bay (by one of Ganga Lor's toadies looking to make a few quick credits, though Skig doesn't know that) and have gone to investigate. He saw at least three ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stormtrooper Recruits"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stormtrooper_Recruits"}," and an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Imperial Junior Officer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Imperial_Junior_Officer","referenceId":"reference:8e94afb25fa1c6c5"}," head toward the docking bay, though he thinks there may be more in the bay. Additionally, Skig saw them moving a repulsor sled into the main docking bay, meaning that they have some heavier weapons at their disposal. With this information in hand, the heroes should be a bit better prepared for the fight ahead of them.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Skig Banos Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +1; ",{"tag":"b","children"